{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790356202,"nonce":"SAGPRqlLfgB6wLrGX6WiIY36hrE=","title":"Function-local static vars were reset on every call","message":"`static var last = 0;` inside a function (Haxe 4.3) parsed as an ordinary local, so it was re-initialised each call (Issue12030 printed AA, want AB; TestLocalStatic, Issue11096 wrong). Fix: the parser marks it, and the type body hoists it to a private static field under the local's name; direct statements, nested blocks, loops, switch cases and try bodies are covered. A name some member already uses, or a static local outside a type body, stays an ordinary local. Conformance 673 -\u003e 676, 0 LOST.","files":null}]}